  { question: 'Do you have to marinate beef jerky?', answer: 'You do not have to marinate beef jerky, but it dramatically improves flavor. The minimum is a dry rub applied 2–4 hours before dehydrating. However, even a quick 4-hour wet marinade adds significantly more flavor depth and moisture than a dry rub alone. For best results, 8–16 hour wet marinating is strongly recommended.' },
